  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAnswers open question 1 of [#2715](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2715) in the five-source common-B mutable-source alphabet of [#1898](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1898): can a multi-connector readout alphabet reach `R\u226478` at `Q=7` with `X=6` after a complete dirty bill?\n\n| Alphabet | Distinct-6 min R | One-repeat R | Tariff at X=6 | Undercuts 436? |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Even-subset (#2686) | 82 | 96 | 442 | no |\n| Dirty shadow (legal) | **82** | 96 | **442** | **no** |\n| Dual indep. same-walk | **82** | 96 | **442** | **no** |\n| Clean shadow (illegal) | **71** | 88 | **420** | yes (not legal) |\n\nDirty shadow collapses to even-subset by sym-diff with the snapshot index. Independent dual same-walk equals even-subset by triangle inequality (`\u03a3_m min_a (e[a]+e[a\u2295m])` machine-checked on all covering sets; not a \u03a3e copy). A dirt-free shadow would undercut, but inherits dirt under PR1898 and fails the dirty bill.\n\n**Scoped obstruction / priced alphabet; no new kappa.** Leave-alone through [#2715](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2715) (including [#2687](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2687), [#2686](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2686), [#2677](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2677), [#2643](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2643), [#2593](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2593)) was not reopened.\n\n## Result\n\nPackage: `research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction/`.\nTip: `cd4ff9427c3e35efb4de09bbf1137e7b68732ecf`.\n\nExact: legal dirty-shadow / dual-indep min R **82** (tariff **442**); illegal clean-shadow min R **71** (tariff **420**); no legal undercut of 436.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction/independent.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction/test_package.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_MULTI_CONNECTOR_7Q_OBSTRUCTION legal_min_R=82 ... answers_cr7q_oq1 no_new_kappa\nPASS_INDEPENDENT_MULTI_CONNECTOR_7Q covering=583296 legal_min=82 ... answers_cr7q_oq1 no_new_kappa\nPASS_MULTI_CONNECTOR_7Q_PACKAGE_TESTS groups=6\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/multi-connector-7q-obstruction outcome=completed\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Admission uses `need()`; `-O` also passes.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest prior: [#2715](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2715) (cr7q OQ1), [#2686](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2686). Freestanding; no competing open PR on this multi-connector/shadow obstruction at refresh.\n\nCredit the mutable-source / #2715 / #2686 / PR1898 lineage. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
